{"id": "EUVD-2026-81750", "enisaUuid": "ce66ff8b-741a-3141-8054-ee4fa8334761", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Reject negative optlen in cgroup getsockopt hook\n\nA cgroup getsockopt BPF program can shrink ctx->optlen after the\nkernel getsockopt handler has run. The kernel-buffer variant, used by\nTCP_ZEROCOPY_RECEIVE, only rejects values larger than the original\nlength.\n\nIf BPF writes a negative optlen, that value is accepted and propagated\nback to the TCP getsockopt code. It can then be passed to\ncopy_to_sockptr() as a size_t and trigger the hardened usercopy\nbytes > INT_MAX warning.\n\nReject negative ctx.optlen in __cgroup_bpf_run_filter_getsockopt_kern(),\nmatching the lower-bound validation already present in the sockptr-based\ngetsockopt hook.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:58:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5b09d984b38b018b123c3a9e02a96bbc6468dbe5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/554ba7195c4108726450e24480c8449990c2268c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d02a12b4085ffe41ea750b1007f7a9c7aee2875a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e6fbf0eba87f50084d67508898f6ad6fc7ff1ba2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f68671b1a98d426c57864bd457c125fee14ac1a5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2bdbe00454200fcb0110f31eeca8d906a3515e74", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31a89af4f513d750fec196e2bb6195a7d4473e9f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b5aacd5b2419b0790e955e466d389a61c79b4b1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90157", "GHSA-v6r2-3cg3-jrp9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0210c477-f6e2-30bd-afce-576ceadef400", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "063a120d-b2fc-3e8e-a15f-d4aba3b81b57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9cacf81f8161111db25f98e78a7a0e32ae142b3f <31a89af4f513d750fec196e2bb6195a7d4473e9f"}, {"id": "233dd77a-7994-3358-a17a-82315292f902", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9cacf81f8161111db25f98e78a7a0e32ae142b3f <1b5aacd5b2419b0790e955e466d389a61c79b4b1"}, {"id": "2b332eb1-b7af-3b9b-a2be-12dbd7a6ecfd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9cacf81f8161111db25f98e78a7a0e32ae142b3f <2bdbe00454200fcb0110f31eeca8d906a3515e74"}, {"id": "37681e82-5b4a-3c9b-9bfe-ca77d05d8300", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "3f9c42d6-c6e4-345d-a5ab-6addd837b987", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.12"}, {"id": "59704b1b-4a0d-3942-a988-3b254f33a8fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9cacf81f8161111db25f98e78a7a0e32ae142b3f <d02a12b4085ffe41ea750b1007f7a9c7aee2875a"}, {"id": "5a27b1d8-bde6-31cc-8e68-5f827d30c725", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "6b42f22b-236b-30d0-b560-b60ad1fa9d1e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "707ce7d9-8174-3062-9f60-2e6a80e47c67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "08f61a34913558e06576e7b6318bf583f273c1be <5b09d984b38b018b123c3a9e02a96bbc6468dbe5"}, {"id": "7fdc8cdb-5aba-3744-99ed-e70be3c329da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "81bbda6c-a8eb-3ba9-ac5b-889914cc5bf0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "a82e4452-9b26-3691-b62b-7057df9e61f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.188 <5.10.270"}, {"id": "bf649610-aee0-3b2a-95ec-6a0d68bb50b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"i